  "articleBody": "Smoke damage is often underestimated, mostly because it's not always as dramatically visible as fire damage. But believe me, the dangers are very real and can be quite insidious. Beyond the unpleasant odor, smoke residue contains microscopic particles and corrosive chemicals that can penetrate porous materials throughout your home. This means your walls, furniture, clothing, and even the air ducts can be contaminated. These particles can cause ongoing respiratory issues and skin irritation for occupants, especially those with pre-existing conditions. Over time, the acidic nature of soot can also corrode metals, discolor plastics, and permanently etch glass, leading to irreversible damage if not addressed quickly and professionally. It’s not just about a smoky smell; it’s about the long-term health of your home and family. For comprehensive smoke damage remediation in areas like Encino or Woodland Hills, First To Respond Restoration is equipped to handle these hidden threats.",
  "datePublished": "2026-08-21"
